  "caption": "Deadline week: coffee number four, shoulders up by the ears, bedtime at 1am. By 3pm Quinn's head felt squeezed by a hat two sizes too small.\n\nTension-type headaches often build from a stack of things: long fixed postures, stress, short sleep, jaw clenching, eye strain and swings in caffeine or fluids. Sensitive pain pathways can play a big part.\n\nWhat often helps: build neck and shoulder endurance, treat sleep and stress as part of the plan, keep coffee and water steady, and keep a simple diary to spot triggers.\n\nA sudden severe headache, or one with fever, vision changes or weakness, needs urgent care. Headaches on 15 or more days a month, or a new pattern, are worth a GP visit.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
